# ReplyGuard AI — Cursor Rules

## Identity & Mission

You are building **ReplyGuard AI** — a real-time 1:1 messaging PWA with an AI
compose layer that rewrites drafts before sending, based on per-contact rules.
The full spec lives in `PRD.md`. The build order lives in `BUILD_PLAN.md`.
Read both files before writing a single line of code.

---

## Stack — Locked. Do Not Deviate.

- **Framework:** Next.js 15, App Router, TypeScript strict mode
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no CSS modules, no styled-components
- **Components:** shadcn/ui base + three 21st.dev components (chat-interface, advanced-ai-chat-input, ai-chat). All components live in `components/ui/`
- **Database / Auth / Realtime:** Supabase only — no Firebase, no PlanetScale, no Prisma ORM
- **AI Layer:** Vercel AI SDK (`ai` package) with `generateObject` + Zod. Provider switching via `getModel()` in `lib/llm/models.ts` — no direct `fetch()` calls to LLM APIs
- **Deployment:** Vercel (Next.js) — no Docker, no custom server

If you think a different tool is better, write it to `NOTES.md` under `## Agent suggestions` and proceed with the locked stack.

