## API Routes — Thin Handlers Only

- API routes (`app/api/**/route.ts`) must contain **no business logic**
- Parse the request, call one lib function, return the response — that's it
- All LLM logic lives in `lib/llm/`, all DB logic lives in `lib/supabase/`
- Example correct pattern:

```typescript
// app/api/ai/rewrite/route.ts
import { rewriteMessage } from "@/lib/llm/rewrite";

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { draft, contactRules, recentHistory } = await req.json();
  const options = await rewriteMessage(draft, contactRules, recentHistory);
  return Response.json({ options });
}
```

---

## AI Layer Rules

- Always use `generateObject` from the `ai` package — never `generateText` for the rewrite endpoint
- The Zod schema must produce exactly 3 options: `z.object({ options: z.array(z.string()).length(3) })`
- Never hardcode a model name — always call `getModel()` from `lib/llm/models.ts`
- Provider is selected by the `LLM_MODEL` env var: `openrouter:<model-id>` or `bedrock:<model-id>`
- Default model when `LLM_MODEL` is unset: `openrouter:deepseek/deepseek-chat`
- Do not add retry logic, streaming, or caching to the rewrite call in v1 — keep it a single `generateObject` call

```typescript
// lib/llm/models.ts — exact implementation, do not refactor
import { createOpenRouter } from "@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider";
import { bedrock } from "@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock";

const openrouter = createOpenRouter({ apiKey: process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY });

export function getModel(name = process.env.LLM_MODEL || "openrouter:deepseek/deepseek-chat") {
  const [provider, ...rest] = name.split(":");
  const modelId = rest.join(":");
  if (provider === "bedrock") return bedrock(modelId);
  return openrouter(modelId);
}
```

