## Scope Enforcement (FPE — Finish Previous version Early)

MVP scope = `PRD.md` section 4 only. The 5 locked features are:

1. Email magic link auth
2. Real-time 1:1 chat
3. AI compose layer (draft → 3 rewrite options → send)
4. Per-contact rules (tone notes, no-send rules, relationship notes)
5. iMessage-style UI

Do not build, scaffold, or stub any of the following in v1:

- Analytics dashboard
- Conversation summaries
- Group chats
- Native iOS / Capacitor wrapper
- Real SMS via Twilio
- Push notifications (APNs)
- Apple Sign In
- Typing indicators beyond basic UI placeholder
- Python/FastAPI rules microservice

If you catch yourself building any of the above, stop immediately, add it to `NOTES.md` under `## v1.1 backlog`, and return to the current `BUILD_PLAN.md` step.

---

## Build Order — Sequential, No Skipping

Execute `BUILD_PLAN.md` steps in this exact order. Do not start a step until the previous step's acceptance check passes:

1. Repo scaffold + 21st.dev components
2. Supabase schema + realtime
3. Auth (magic link)
4. Conversation list `/chats`
5. Thread view `/chats/[id]` + realtime delivery
6. AI compose layer (the core feature)
7. Contact profile `/chats/[id]/profile` + rules
8. Local end-to-end test
9. PWA manifest + Vercel deploy

After each step: run the app, confirm no errors, tell the user what to manually test, then stop and wait for explicit go-ahead before continuing.

